; DOMAIN: perfectoid-spaces [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-24]
; Claim: A perfectoid ring (Scholze, Fontaine) is a complete Tate ring R over Q_p (or a p-complete ring) with a pseudo-uniformizer pi such that pi^p divides p, R is uniform, and the Frobenius phi: R/p -> R/p, x |-> x^p is surjective (an isomorphism on R^o/p). The tilting equivalence sends R to its tilt R^flat = lim_{x->x^p} R, a perfectoid ring of characteristic p, with R^flat = lim R/p as a multiplicative monoid; the Fontaine map sharp: R^flat -> R recovers R. The tilting correspondence is an equivalence of categories between perfectoid rings/algebras over R and over R^flat, and (Almost Purity / Faltings) preserves finite etale sites: R_fet ~ R^flat_fet, the arithmetic-to-geometric bridge underlying p-adic Hodge theory. Almost mathematics (Gabber-Ramero) works modulo the ideal m of the almost-zero elements (killed by pi^{1/p^infty}) so that the cotangent complex of a perfectoid vanishes almost. Perfectoid rings are precisely the base rings that carry a canonical prism: R perfectoid <=> (A_inf(R), ker theta) is a perfect prism, with theta: A_inf = W(R^flat) -> R the Fontaine map; this is the input to prismatic/BMS integral p-adic Hodge theory.
; Bridge: genesis_prismatic_cohomology (perfectoid rings are exactly those with a perfect prism (A_inf(R)=W(R^flat), ker theta); the tilt R^flat and Fontaine theta ARE the delta-ring/ideal data of the prism, so perfectoids are the base geometry underlying prismatic cohomology and BMS) + genesis_k_theory (perfectoid/A_inf inputs feed the motivic filtration and p-adic K-theory computations via the cyclotomic trace) + genesis_sheaf_cohomology (the tilting equivalence is an equivalence of finite-etale sites R_fet ~ R^flat_fet, almost-purity, giving the pro-etale/sheaf comparison for p-adic cohomology).
(= (perfectoid-ring $R) (complete-tate-ring $R (pseudo-uniformizer $pi) (divides (power $pi $p) $p) (surjective (frobenius (quotient $R $p)))))
(= (tilt $R) (inverse-limit (frobenius-tower $R) (map $x (power $x $p))))
(= (fontaine-theta $R) (map (witt-vectors (tilt $R)) $R))
(= (a-inf $R) (witt-vectors (tilt $R)))
(= (perfect-prism $R) (prism (a-inf $R) (kernel (fontaine-theta $R))))
(= (tilting-equivalence $R) (equivalence (perfectoid-algebras $R) (perfectoid-algebras (tilt $R))))
(= (almost-purity $R) (equivalence (finite-etale-site $R) (finite-etale-site (tilt $R))))
(= (almost-zero $x) (killed-by $x (ideal (roots $pi (power $p infinity)))))